Optimal Solution - Find the kth largest element by maintaining a min-heap of size k while iterating through the array.

class Solution {
    public int findKthLargest(int[] nums, int k) {
        // Min-heap to keep track of the k largest elements
        PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();
        // Process each number in the array
        for (int num : nums) {
            // Add current number to the heap
            pq.offer(num);
            // If heap size exceeds k, remove the smallest element
            // This ensures the heap always contains the k largest elements
            if (pq.size() > k) {
                pq.poll();
            }
        }
        // The top of the min-heap is the kth largest element
        return pq.peek();
    }
}


Time Complexity :- O(n log k).
Space Complexity :- O(k).
